seg-55cf42830155 = Kshana Studio is the web app built on the WebAssembly build, so a Studio view exists where the WASM column has an entry point, and where it does not the cell points to a <b>Command line card</b> (the command to run, with its arguments), never to a result Studio computed. Pages (kshana.dev/studio/, client-side): <b>Maritime trust</b> (<c1/>), <b>Training debrief</b> (<c2/>), <b>Interference map</b> (<c3/>), <b>Geometry</b> (<c4/>: a representative skyplot, skyline, DOP, error ellipse and Monte Carlo cloud from the engine; { "0.36" }), <b>Lunar station</b> (<c5/>: the modelled coverage of a lunar reference station from the <c6/> kind; { "0.36" }) and the <b>Tools</b> page, whose sections are OSNMA (<c7/>), Evidence packs (<c8/>), Test-bench export (<c9/>), Compliance mapping (<c10/>), the Command line tab (telemetry card, IQ, marine integrations: commands to run) and Use from your AI assistant (<c11/>). A <c12/> in the Studio column of the subcommand table is a command that is not one of the { "0.35" } capabilities Studio presents.

